---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import DiagramGallery from '../components/DiagramGallery.astro';import MappingStudio from '../components/MappingStudio.astro';import GraphExplorer from '../components/GraphExplorer.astro';import DomainSwitcher from '../components/DomainSwitcher.astro';
const pages={vision:['Vision & positioning','From fragmented records to a governed understanding of enterprise operations.'],architecture:['Solution architecture','A modular, ontology-first design with explicit trust boundaries and canonical persistence.'],'data-lifecycle':['Data lifecycle','A controlled CSV ingestion journey: profile, map, approve, validate, commit, and project.'],ontology:['Dynamic ontology engine','Versioned business schemas define entities, properties, relationships, and allowed actions.'],intelligence:['AI intelligence','A governed agent plans with approved tools and responds using authorized evidence.'],security:['Security & governance','Identity, workspace isolation, policy checks, audit, and human approvals.'],'product-preview':['Product UI concepts','Explore the proposed workspaces and product experiences; these are not connected to a backend.'],developers:['Developer documentation','Proposed stack, APIs, architecture decisions, and development standards.'],roadmap:['Roadmap & release gates','A transparent view of what is designed, planned, and still to be built.']};
export function getStaticPaths(){return ['vision','architecture','data-lifecycle','ontology','intelligence','security','product-preview','developers','roadmap'].map(slug=>({params:{slug}}))}
const slug=Astro.params.slug!;const [title,desc]=(pages as Record<string,[string,string]>)[slug];
const galleries:Record<string,string[][]>={architecture:[['01','System context & trust boundaries'],['02','Modular component architecture'],['10','Local / private deployment topology'],['12','Domain-independent core']], 'data-lifecycle':[['03','CSV ingestion & decision flow'],['04','One row to canonical objects'],['11','Ingestion sequence & transactional outbox']],ontology:[['05','Ontology registry lifecycle'],['04','Source-to-ontology transformation']],intelligence:[['06','Governed agent query execution']],security:[['07','Workspace isolation & authorization'],['08','Sensitive action approval workflow']],'product-preview':[['09','Portal information architecture']]};
---
<Base title={title}><div class="container"><header class="pagehead"><div class="eyebrow">Krita / Internal knowledge portal · Proposed</div><h1>{title}</h1><p class="lead">{desc}</p></header>{galleries[slug]&&<DiagramGallery items={galleries[slug]}/>}<div class="content">{slug==='vision'&&<><h2>Why Krita?</h2><p>Krita (कृत) evokes something accomplished or well-formed, with inspiration from Krita Yuga's association with truth and order. Its promise is to create structural clarity from complex enterprise data.</p><div class="notice">Krita is an independent proposed product inspired by observable enterprise intelligence patterns. It does not claim access to proprietary Palantir technology.</div><h2>From data chaos to structural intelligence</h2><p>Normalize disconnected records, connect relationships with a versioned ontology, retrieve evidence under policy, and execute only approved actions.</p><DomainSwitcher/></>}{slug==='architecture'&&<><h2>Eight logical layers</h2><div class="flowsteps">{['Source connectivity','Data processing','Storage & indexing','Ontology & metadata','Operational actions','AI intelligence','API & identity','Experience'].map(x=><span class="step">{x}</span>)}</div><h2>Core design decisions</h2><p>PostgreSQL is the canonical system of record for objects, links, lineage, approvals and outbox events. Neo4j is a derived index. LangGraph orchestrates typed tools; Azure AI Foundry is the proposed initial inference provider.</p><p>These are logical responsibilities and need not map to independent microservices.</p></>}{slug==='data-lifecycle'&&<><h2>CSV onboarding sequence</h2><div class="flowsteps">{['Stage & profile','Review ontology','Suggest mapping','Human approval','Validate / quarantine','Commit + outbox','Project graph','Publish lineage'].map(x=><span class="step">{x}</span>)}</div><MappingStudio/><h2>Ingestion invariants</h2><p>Import identity is workspace-scoped. Repeat imports must be idempotent. Invalid rows are quarantined with reasons. Canonical changes and outbox events commit atomically, while graph projection is asynchronous and may lag.</p></>}{slug==='ontology'&&<><h2>Ontology contracts</h2><p>Entity types, keys, properties, relationship cardinality, classification, and allowed actions are versioned. Breaking changes require a migration and rollback plan.</p><pre>{`Patient (patient_id) --HAS_ENCOUNTER--> Encounter (encounter_id)
Encounter --ATTENDED_BY--> Provider
Encounter --AT_FACILITY--> Facility
Encounter --HAS_DIAGNOSIS--> Diagnosis`}</pre><h2>Registry lifecycle</h2><div class="flowsteps">{['Draft','Validate','Review','Publish immutable version','Migration plan','Activate','Discover tools'].map(x=><span class="step">{x}</span>)}</div><GraphExplorer/></>}{slug==='intelligence'&&<><h2>Authorized tools, not arbitrary queries</h2><p>Universal tool proposals include <code>list_entity_types</code>, <code>get_entity_schema</code>, <code>query_entities</code>, <code>get_entity</code>, <code>traverse_relationships</code>, and <code>get_source_lineage</code>.</p><div class="notice">The LLM plans. Trusted application code validates tool inputs, applies policy, performs bounded queries, and returns traceable evidence. No live model is connected to this portal.</div><h2>Example investigation</h2><p>“Show all encounters for P001, involved providers, and repeat visits within 30 days.” The proposed application would compute dates deterministically and cite encounter IDs without inventing clinical conclusions.</p></>}{slug==='security'&&<><h2>Policy before retrieval</h2><p>Workspace membership must be established from authenticated identity. PostgreSQL row-level security and application authorization enforce boundaries. Neo4j Community predicates alone are not strong tenant isolation.</p><h2>Human-in-the-loop action control</h2><div class="flowsteps">{['Propose','Authorize','Approve','Revalidate','Execute','Audit'].map(x=><span class="step">{x}</span>)}</div><div class="notice">All healthcare data on this site is synthetic. Do not upload PHI or confidential production banking data. Real deployment requires privacy, legal, security and cloud-region review.</div></>}{slug==='product-preview'&&<><h2>Planned screens</h2><div class="grid3">{['Workspace dashboard','Data Mapping Studio','Ontology Registry','Graph Explorer','AI Investigation Workspace','Approval Center','Ingestion Job Monitor','Audit Trail'].map(x=><div class="card"><span class="pill">Concept</span><h3>{x}</h3><p>Proposed product experience. No connected operational backend.</p></div>)}</div><h2>Interactive previews</h2><MappingStudio/><GraphExplorer/></>}{slug==='developers'&&<><h2>Proposed technology stack</h2><table><tbody>{[['Portal','Astro, TypeScript, static HTML/CSS'],['Future API','Python 3.12+, FastAPI, Pydantic, SQLAlchemy'],['Canonical store','PostgreSQL + transactional outbox'],['Graph index','Neo4j via trusted query gateway'],['AI orchestration','LangGraph + Azure AI Foundry inference'],['Quality','pytest, Playwright, OpenTelemetry']].map(([a,b])=><tr><th>{a}</th><td>{b}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><h2>Future API contract (not implemented)</h2><pre>{`POST /api/v1/workspaces
POST /api/v1/ontology/publish
POST /api/v1/ingestion/csv/profile
POST /api/v1/ingestion/mappings
POST /api/v1/ingestion/jobs
GET  /api/v1/entities
GET  /api/v1/graph/neighbors
POST /api/v1/agents/query`}</pre><h2>Engineering decisions</h2><p>Workspace isolation tier, production identity provider, entity resolution, retention, graph deployment, cloud region and hosting policy remain open. Record decisions as versioned ADRs before implementation.</p></>}{slug==='roadmap'&&<><h2>Phased delivery</h2><div class="grid2">{[['01','Internal knowledge portal','This deliverable: static documentation, diagrams and synthetic browser demos.'],['02','Core foundation','Identity, PostgreSQL, registry APIs and tests.'],['03','Data mapping backend','CSV profiling, approved mappings and idempotent ingestion.'],['04','Relationship intelligence','Neo4j derived projection and lineage.'],['05','AI intelligence','Foundry adapter, LangGraph tools and grounded evaluations.'],['06','Pulse demonstration','Synthetic healthcare end-to-end demo.'],['07','Ledger demonstration','Second ontology without core code changes.'],['08','Hardening','Approvals, isolation, observability and threat modeling.']].map(([n,h,p])=><div class="card"><span class="pill">{n==='01'?'Portal prototype':'Planned'}</span><h3>{n} · {h}</h3><p>{p}</p></div>)}</div><h2>Verification criteria</h2><p>Working portal navigation, diagram rendering, interactive mapping, synthetic graph inspection and production build are portal release checks. Backend functionality requires separate integration and security tests before it can be marked implemented or verified.</p></>}</div></div></Base>
